-- 7. reviews 
INSERT INTO "public"."reviews" ("id", "trainee_id", "reviewer_id", "review_type", "review_period", "rating", "strengths", "areas_for_improvement", "recommendation", "reviewed_at", "created_at", "updated_at", "mt_reply", "mt_reply_at") VALUES ('81cc50fb-b108-4648-b4ac-887972e25919', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'fffa07ae-27f0-4145-9c2b-5a332d446e0f', 'encouragement', '2026-07-15', null, null, null, 'Hi, Ishi, I would LIKE to summarize some of the points we discussed OVER the past couple of days. I hope putting them into writing will help you better understand AND remember them AS you continue your journey
WITH MATTA. 1. The biggest difference BETWEEN school AND the workplace The biggest difference BETWEEN campus life AND working life is that, IN the workplace, you need to use your professional knowledge, your attitude toward solving problems, your communication skills, AND your personal character to work
WITH people who have different backgrounds, personalities, AND ways of thinking. Together, you

CREATE value for the company while also building your own experience, capabilities, AND career. Of course, you also earn an income that allows you to pursue the life you want. Work is not only about making a living—it''s also about continuously investing IN yourself. 2. Teamwork is important, but you are still responsible for your own growth While teamwork is essential, never forget that you are the main person responsible for your own development. No one else can replace your attitude, your willingness to learn, or your determination to improve. Learn how to work well
WITH others, but also learn how to manage yourself. 3. Great achievements are never accomplished alone No major project is completed by one person alone. Every successful project is the result of people
WITH different expertise working together toward the same goal. WHEN everyone contributes their strengths, the result is far greater than what any individual could achieve alone. The important question, then, is not "How can I do everything myself?" but rather: "How can I earn the trust and willingness of others to work with me?" This is actually one of the central ideas behind many of the lessons I share—how to gain support, build trust, AND

CREATE collaboration. 4. MATTA is developing future leaders, not only professionals MATTA is not only designed to develop technical or professional expertise. More importantly, we hope to cultivate future managers AND leaders who can organize, inspire, AND develop teams. For this reason, besides strengthening your own professional capability, we will continue emphasizing teamwork, communication, leadership, AND the ability to develop others. A great leader is not someone who can do everything alone, but someone who can help others grow. WHEN knowledge AND capability can be shared AND multiplied, the entire team becomes stronger. 5. Keep improving yourself Professional knowledge is important, but it is only one part of your development. Continue improving your: . Professional competence . Problem-solving ability . Communication skills . EQ . Humility AND professionalism . Respect for others . Learning attitude These qualities will determine how far you can grow IN your career. 6. Don''t become a work machine Everything we teach IN MATTA is not intended to turn you into a work machine that only chases targets AND performance. These skills are simply tools to help you build the life you want. Every experience you gain today is preparing you to become a better version of yourself. The more knowledge, experience, AND wisdom you accumulate, the more choices you will have IN designing your own future. Our goal is not simply to build successful employees—it is to help you build a successful life. Finally, I hope you will always stay curious, observe more, learn continuously, AND be willing to change. Every morning we give you time to read industry news, AI developments, business updates, AND even political AND economic news. The purpose is not simply to increase your knowledge, but to help you develop a broader perspective. The world is changing rapidly. Future leaders cannot focus only
ON their own department or technical field—they need to understand the world around them. One last reminder: This is no longer school. Don''t wait for someone to tell you what you should learn. Take the initiative. Ask questions. Observe. Learn. Improve yourself every day. If you can become just a little better than yesterday, you''re already moving IN the right direction. Let''s keep learning AND growing together. ^_^', '2026-07-15 01:13:24.26391+00', '2026-07-15 01:13:24.26391+00', '2026-07-15 03:40:00.91809+00', 'Hello Sir Yangson, Thank you for the encouragement, feedback, AND summary; I will make sure to take these to heart AS I go
ON my journey towards being a better employee AND person. I''m aiming for the goal of trusting myself more AS an individual AND to stop doubting myself because that is something that I have been struggling about for a very long time. I look forward to what MATTA AND my future experiences will make me discover about myself AND my own capabilities, I am inexperienced AS this is my first job but I will do my best every day. Again, thank you very much!', '2026-07-15 03:40:00.91809+00')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;


-- 8. training_records 
INSERT INTO "public"."training_records" ("id", "trainee_id", "course_id", "attendance_date", "attended", "test_score", "reflection", "completion_status", "created_at", "updated_at", "hours") VALUES ('01f1e5ca-405e-43ae-98bf-b7db238bbdfa', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '5d6803e2-90cc-43fe-8ca5-c7e9c7f0f4a6', '2026-08-17', true, null, 'Notes: Course 1 covered Browave’s company background AND product line-up. Founded IN 1998 IN Taiwan AND expanded to Subic IN 2022, Browave manufactures fiber optic components across two (soon to be 3) product lines (PD1, PD2, PD3 (soon)) used IN telecom AND datacom applications such AS splitters, WDM filters, fiber arrays, AND connectors. The session also introduced the MATTA program itself, which grew out of the earlier Manager Associate Program (MAP) AND combines a structured core curriculum, specialized training, leadership development, AND even Chinese language learning, along
WITH external training opportunities AND clear career pathways. It closed
WITH an overview of the company’s administrative departments, including HR, Material Resources, Production Material Control, Finance, Production, Quality Assurance, AND Industrial Engineering. Reflection: Knowing the company’s product lines AND department structure gives me a map of
WHERE my work AS a trainee will eventually fit in. Since MATTA is built around rotating through core curriculum, specialized training,
AND leadership development, understanding departments LIKE QA, Production, Industrial Engineering,
AND Production Material Control now will make it easier to see how my future rotations
AND responsibilities connect to the bigger picture, instead of treating each department AS an isolated stop. It also reminded me that this program is not only about learning the technical side of the business, but about preparing me to eventually combine self-expectations 
WITH on-the-job performance, which is the same direction-setting mindset Sir Yangson kept emphasizing.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:12:24.307513+00', '2026-08-21 00:46:12.097219+00', '1.0'), ('02d27ff8-7378-4a0a-ba56-fcb328ac302e', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '8638970f-981e-454a-86cb-c9c831647ad0', '2026-08-13', true, null, 'I learned about the operation of the Dimension 3D Testing Machine AND the 3D test forms.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-14 07:26:37.170183+00', '2026-08-14 07:27:44.649621+00', '8.0'), ('03b3ee13-3347-4b94-ade2-af7257143a3a', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'c7c9b82b-1e47-4d98-b37a-39e368dda657', '2026-08-04', true, null, 'I learned about ribbonization basics AND practiced.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-06 08:56:00.265819+00', '2026-08-06 08:56:00.265819+00', '8.0'), ('04914e41-09ef-4556-8cb1-1082f9181458', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '532605ce-fde7-4cf9-ab4b-2b8bcbb28a4f', '2026-08-21', true, null, 'Notes: This course covered how to write effective reports at three different cadences: daily, weekly, AND monthly. Daily reports should cover work IN progress, problems or abnormalities, AND tomorrow''s priorities, AND should write the result rather than only the action taken. For example, summarizing 3 applicable points
FROM a training attended, following a "Correct, Prevent, Report" (CPR) approach. Weekly reports follow the "Progress + Issues + Next Action" format: what changed (concrete output produced AND progress made against the work plan), what needs attention (issues, confusion, delays, or risks that require clarification or support), AND what comes next (next week''s plan AND outstanding follow-ups), always highlighting what genuinely matters, giving exact numbers, AND including follow-ups, open questions, AND recommendations. Monthly reports shift the focus to reviewing whether monthly targets were achieved, specifying numbers, summaries, follow-ups, AND key learnings, AND running everything through a "highlight → give number → follow-up → question → recommend" chain, while also addressing core content AND management value. Across all three report format, the same writing principles apply: start
WITH the result, write outcomes rather than activities, use facts AND data, AND always include the next action. Reflection: Seeing daily, weekly, AND monthly reporting laid out together made it clear these aren''t three separate skills, they''re the same "Progress + Issues + Next Action" habit applied at different levels. AS a MATTA trainee, that reframes how I should think about my own reporting: my daily notes should already be written so they roll up cleanly into a weekly report, AND my weekly reports should be building blocks I can compress into a monthly one, rather than each being written
FROM scratch. The "write the result, not the action" rule AND the CPR habit hit too close to home for the daily report, since what I do before is AS easy AS a saying "I attended X" instead of asking what actually changed because of it. The monthly report''s focus
ON management value is also a good reminder of how the audience shifts AS reports move up the chain: a supervisor reading my daily note mainly wants to know I''m
ON track, but by the time something reaches management it needs to already answer "so what" for the business, meaning the number, the follow-up, AND the recommendation all have to be built in, not left unknown.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-22 06:01:58.026321+00', '2026-08-22 06:28:59.612789+00', '1.0'), ('072cb317-c0f8-4662-a590-79005fdd402a', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '3d455a85-5a84-491b-81d3-ca96298f32ae', '2026-08-21', true, null, 'Notes: This course gave an overview of the optical communications industry, which serves AS the backbone of today''s internet, cloud computing, AND 5G/6G networks. It covered how the technology works end to end: data is converted
FROM an electrical signal into an optical (laser) signal for transmission through fiber, THEN converted back
FROM optical to electrical signal
ON the receiving end. It traced the industry''s timeline
FROM invention of the laser IN the 1960s, through low-loss optical fiber IN the 1970s, commercial fiber-optic networks replacing copper cable IN the 1980s, internet AND broadband expansion IN the 1990s, FTTx IN the 2000s, the cloud computing era IN the 2010s, AND AI AND next-gen networks
FROM 2020 onward, arriving at
WHERE the industry stands IN 2026: mainstream speeds of 800 Gb/s, an expected jump to 1TB/s,
AND emerging developments LIKE silicon photonics, co-package optics, 6G integration,
AND hollow-core fiber for lower latency. It closed 
WITH the Philippine context (5G, FTTx, AI & Cloud, national connectivity), the major local industry players (PLDT, DITO, Globe, Converge, Eastern Communications), AND the smart city hubs driving this infrastructure (IT Hub Cebu, BGC, Makati, New Clark City). Reflection: This course zoomed out
FROM the softer, process-oriented topics of the week into the actual physical infrastructure that makes all of it possible, AND it was a useful reminder that even the most abstract-feeling business processes I''ve been learning ultimately run
ON top of real, physical technology LIKE fiber AND lasers. AS a MATTA trainee, I don''t need to become a telecom engineer, but knowing the basic timeline AND vocabulary of the industry, terms LIKE FTTx, co-package optics, or hollow-core fiber, means I can follow a conversation or a slide deck about infrastructure without getting lost, AND I can better appreciate why national connectivity AND smart city development (Cebu, BGC, Makati, New Clark City) are treated AS strategic priorities rather than just technical footnotes. It also reinforced how fast this space moves: what counted AS cutting-edge a decade ago (FTTx, cloud) is now baseline, AND the industry is already planning for 6G AND terabit speeds, which is a good reminder to keep learning continuously rather than assuming what I know today stays relevant indefinitely.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-22 06:37:05.93415+00', '2026-08-22 06:37:05.93415+00', '2.0'), ('0a0579cb-a193-4603-92cf-371d786a0470', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '920332a0-9aa1-473d-a34b-a34452befe47', '2026-07-16', true, null, 'On the Topic of AI: "US official says Nvidia has begun shipping powerful H200 AI chips to China" - Jeffrey Kessler said that the shipping of the product to China is ''very few''. Though export controls are still under scrutiny AS Trump "has turned export controls into a bargaining chip in negotiations with China". Link: https://www.reuters.com/world/china/us-official-says-shipments-h200-chips-china-have-begun-2026-07-14/ Reflections: US AND China are still rivals IN terms of tech, I think they will continue to be this way.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-16 00:07:16.889273+00', '2026-07-16 00:07:16.889273+00', '1.0'), ('0d1dee06-8d95-4d90-af3f-be45dab04d85', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '075ced4b-39b3-4538-9bec-567def81487a', '2026-07-16', true, null, 'I learned about the processes IN the Production Department, their key indicators, standards AND what formulas are being used to get the numbers.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-16 07:57:03.015526+00', '2026-07-16 07:57:03.015526+00', '2.0'), ('0d2eecb5-bf35-4a2b-bd5e-90f6b6975ab9', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '60ff127b-dd87-46b6-a328-b521f4893cf5', '2026-08-17', true, null, 'I 3D tested products AND recorded them
