FROM happening again by making changes.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-24 06:36:40.12895+00', '2026-07-24 06:36:40.12895+00', '1.5'), ('1ae12ad2-019d-4737-942f-e9c9a15753ba', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'd989088b-313f-47d4-983f-a3426a84518a', '2026-07-24', true, null, 'Here I learned more about the 5M1E, 4M change management, work IN progress AND yield calculations.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-24 09:03:24.955878+00', '2026-07-24 09:03:24.955878+00', '2.0'), ('1b7e0848-4321-4bda-ab02-1027130ddc43', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '83204ea2-b5be-44a5-99d4-4e5915dd53f1', '2026-08-10', true, null, 'I learned about polishing AND its five stages.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-13 08:37:51.437766+00', '2026-08-13 08:39:46.602837+00', '8.0'), ('1c904362-a9f7-4af5-afaa-e7f76324db5c', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', 'ce1c8b44-0f84-48b7-8096-bc21767b0531', '2026-08-19', true, null, 'Notes: This course introduced how the warehouse function fits into Browave’s operations, covering raw materials, finished products, AND the importance of inventory accuracy (targeting 100% accuracy for customer satisfaction). It walked through the full process flow,
FROM supplier to receiving AND inspection, storage, inventory management, material issuance to production, the production process itself, finished goods receiving, packing AND labeling, AND finally shipping to the customer. It also covered the warehouse’s main functions (receiving, storage, material issuance, finished goods, shipping), the departments it collaborates
WITH (Production Technology, CBA, Finance, Planning, AND Quality Control), AND the “5 Rights of Warehouse”: right material, right quantity, right location, right time, AND right quality. Reflection: Seeing the warehouse process laid out step by step made me realize how much cross-departmental coordination happens before a product even reaches production, let alone the customer. AS a MATTA trainee rotating through different areas, I think the “5 Rights” framework is something I can apply well beyond the warehouse itself, since getting the right thing, IN the right amount, IN the right place, at the right time, AND at the right quality is really just a specific version of the direction-and-goal-setting mindset
FROM Sir Yangson’s sessions. It is a reminder that even routine, process-heavy work still depends on
HAVING a clear target before acting.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:41:27.53632+00', '2026-08-21 05:16:34.827567+00', '2.0'), ('2164e5c1-afeb-4805-a797-cb8598a02f08', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '9bdc5d59-25bd-44be-8463-26e8c2bdec51', '2026-07-15', true, null, 'On the topic of Economy: The US-Iran war had a greater effect than expected
ON Philippine Economy AS the IMF further decreased its growth projections for the Philippines
FROM 4.1% to 3.9%. This is further demonstrated by the sudden spike of oil prices AND other goods across the country. Link: https://mb.com.ph/2026/07/08/philippine-economy-takes-bigger-than-expected-hit-from-us-iran-warimf Reflection: This shows how much the US-Iran war is affecting other nations. The war just keeps getting worse AS the time passes now that the US is striking Iran again for closing the Strait of Hormuz.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-15 00:15:51.325876+00', '2026-07-15 00:16:08.035846+00', '1.0'), ('22774c0a-f513-4c57-bac0-5df54dc1865f', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'fb9cfdf1-9c3d-4c72-ab84-ce6827fd7dad', '2026-07-28', true, null, 'I learned about the general process IN the MPO, including the workflow. I observed AND learned how to do the cutting AND winding process.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-05 09:12:12.552801+00', '2026-08-05 09:12:12.552801+00', '8.0'), ('22c887be-4c50-4d62-bbe3-ac7c71768de9', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '0aac3136-e839-465d-aa1f-841b9259ab40', '2026-08-24', true, null, 'Notes: The session focused
ON bridging Chinese AND Western workplace cultures IN a Taiwanese company through four themes: understand, adapt, connect, AND grow. Chinese workplace culture is shaped by Confucian values such AS respect for elders, harmony, group interests, family responsibility, AND humility, contrasting
WITH the more individualistic AND direct Western approach. The concept of “face” is important, meaning criticism should be given privately AND disagreements are often expressed indirectly. Trust, or guanxi, is built gradually through shared meals, favors, AND consistent support. IN the workplace, seniority is respected, bosses typically speak last, AND decisions are followed publicly while concerns are discussed privately. Long hours may also demonstrate commitment, while SOPs are expected to be followed closely. Taiwanese workplace norms emphasize punctuality, humility, teamwork, frequent reporting, AND maintaining both speed AND quality. Practical behaviors include greeting seniors first, saying “OK, I’ll try,” reporting problems early, joining team activities, AND learning basic Mandarin. Publicly challenging a boss, bluntly refusing tasks or overtime, leaving without informing others, AND openly gossiping or complaining should be avoided. The session also highlighted similarities BETWEEN Filipino AND Taiwanese cultures, particularly respect for family AND elders, harmony, AND hard work. However, differences IN punctuality, public behavior, AND attitudes toward social activities AND religion require greater awareness. Overall, the session showed that cultural understanding is essential for adapting, building relationships, communicating effectively, AND succeeding IN a Taiwanese workplace. Reflection: AS a Management Associate Trainee (MATTA) at Browave, this lecture gave me a practical perspective
ON how I should conduct myself IN a Taiwanese workplace. I realized that understanding the importance of harmony, seniority, AND indirect communication can help me avoid unintentionally appearing disrespectful or confrontational. The differences IN working hours, decision-making, AND SOP compliance also helped me understand that commitment may be shown through visible effort, respect for authority, AND careful adherence to established procedures. What stood out to me most were the simple practices I can apply immediately, such AS reporting problems early, responding
WITH “OK, I’ll try,” AND participating IN team meals AND activities. These small actions can help me build trust AND strengthen my relationships
WITH colleagues. I also appreciated the similarities BETWEEN Filipino AND Taiwanese values, particularly our respect for family AND elders, sense of harmony, AND strong work ethic. At the same time, I need to be more mindful of differences IN punctuality, public behavior, AND social habits. Overall, the lecture reminded me that adapting to a new workplace is not about changing who I am, but about understanding AND respecting a different way of working. AS I begin my traineeship, I hope to apply these lessons to communicate better, build meaningful relationships, AND grow into a more culturally aware professional.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-24 04:00:55.011348+00', '2026-08-24 04:50:32.816878+00', '1.0'), ('232130ab-4dc9-41d4-9f87-d6c7f0390c7c', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '3f6c8479-2a30-4fa0-a668-1e5e5909fd79', '2026-08-03', true, null, 'I learned about more standards AND procedure
ON the batch feeding procedure.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-06 08:54:06.4558+00', '2026-08-06 08:54:06.4558+00', '8.0'), ('26549760-dc5d-483d-9c5f-472022b8b053', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'c3e6b957-8684-4b4e-9cb0-0aaf16a2d4e5', '2026-07-22', true, null, 'On the topic of Politics: "New strikes as Trump warns Iran will pay for US troop deaths" Link: https://www.philstar.com/world/2026/07/21/2543635/new-strikes-trump-warns-iran-will-pay-us-troop-deaths Reflection: This war is tiring to hear about AS none of them are willing to stop launching strikes. I hope it ends already.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-22 00:20:12.730702+00', '2026-07-22 00:20:12.730702+00', '1.0'), ('2b39e03f-bb6e-432c-a166-158b2a757055', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '920332a0-9aa1-473d-a34b-a34452befe47', '2026-07-14', true, null, 'On the Topic of AI: "A Korean research team has developed a technology that enables the stable stacking of more than 10 ultrathin semiconductor chips, each only one-fifth the thickness of a human hair." Link: https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/technology/this-new-chip-stacking-technique-could-be-the-key-to-unlocking-faster-ai-performance/ar-AA27KX0k?ocid = msedgntphdr&cvid = a2b40d8e95914c388233d7f3f13d1849&cvpid = 3c230cea25d24cfef202cf4c39f51927&ei = 14 Reflection: This breakthrough IN technology makes room for a lot more productivity AND improvement IN AI performance.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-14 01:13:07.990432+00', '2026-07-14 01:36:46.765049+00', '1.0'), ('30e26464-ae29-41e5-86ea-6d2def1e3eab', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'a783e427-a345-4de7-a2cf-3226e80a20de', '2026-07-17', true, null, 'Here, I learned about the 5M1E analysis, its elements, AND how it is used IN real-life situations to identify root causes.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-17 07:20:08.690301+00', '2026-07-17 07:20:08.690301+00', '1.5'), ('32788319-7396-4de3-8db8-cfac9a54209a', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'dfa8237a-b7f9-4e54-8016-e1e219e16702', '2026-08-11', true, null, 'I learned about the SG machine AND the maintenance AND monitoring forms, AND the glue dispensing machine.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-13 08:40:45.899158+00', '2026-08-13 08:42:08.23263+00', '8.0'), ('399e39d0-f2ea-44af-a932-f4699c4ef3a3', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '9ce83cec-d0df-4047-a290-f4150532f7ae', '2026-07-31', true, null, 'I learned about the parts used AND the procedures for batch feeding.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-06 08:52:43.731581+00', '2026-08-06 08:52:43.731581+00', '8.0'), ('3a6e0a7d-4f8b-4daa-874c-5d08aaa555b3', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'f4545581-5ce3-45cf-94c2-67380dfaa5cb', '2026-07-17', true, null, 'Here I learned about how optical communications correlates
WITH AI AND how it is basically mandatory for today''s standards AND demands.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-17 03:59:39.434352+00', '2026-07-17 04:39:17.367576+00', '2.0'), ('4e8a5aa0-0c73-4df4-9691-88509daf2017', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '4c1ecdc9-82bd-4281-be02-c922c20f96c9', '2026-08-21', true, null, 'Notes: Course 12, Five Things IN the Office, focused
ON practical workplace survival skills beyond technical know-how. It opened
WITH a “Law of the Jungle” analogy, competition for survival applied to the office, AND five Office Survival Rules: time management, emotional management, keeping a professional distance IN socializing, observation skills AND adaptability (including reading a supervisor’s personality AND working style), AND focusing
ON work performance through Target + Schedule + Index, which we apply PDCA (plan, do, check, act) to. The core of the session THEN covered five specific skills: writing effective emails (clear subject lines, the correct use of CC versus BCC, AND USING email AS evidence WHEN clarifying instructions); understanding the difference BETWEEN “did” (process only) AND “done” (process plus experience gained), AND always asking for feedback to build trust; writing clear reports that present solutions USING SWOT for a supervisor’s approval, rather than just raising problems; developing the habit of achieving goals; AND communicating effectively through flowcharts, the 5W1H method, active listening, clear body language, AND feedback. It closed
WITH a side piece of advice: don’t show that you know everything. Reflection: This session felt LIKE the practical, day-to-day counterpart to Sir Yangson’s earlier talks
ON choice AND direction. Those sessions gave me the big-picture mindset, AND this one gave me specific behaviors to apply it. AS a MATTA trainee reporting closely to supervisors AND executives, skills LIKE writing clear emails, knowing WHEN to CC versus BCC, AND turning problems into report-ready solutions USING SWOT are things I can start practicing immediately rather than waiting until I have a formal role. The “did versus done” distinction also reframes how I should treat every training task: not just finishing something, but being able to articulate what I actually learned
FROM it, which ties directly back to the Learning Portfolio AND reflection summaries built into the MATTA program. Above all, understanding my supervisor’s personality AND working style, AND asking for feedback to build trust, feels LIKE the most immediately useful skill for succeeding IN a program
WHERE I am expected to work closely 
WITH people far more experienced than me.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 03:08:38.779684+00', '2026-08-22 06:03:19.781713+00', '1.5'), ('55f222a6-d8bd-42a0-8e25-b21399dabd7f', '328b3986-dbff-442e-9818-b13683cbbb1e', '3f7ec78a-2a86-448d-87e9-282ca72f8ca7', '2026-07-09', true, '100.00', 'rrrr', 'in_progress', '2026-07-09 07:12:18.035223+00', '2026-07-09 07:12:18.035223+00', '1.0'), ('56ede463-e7d6-48ab-b1c2-da8660d9134b', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'af08767d-a625-43ca-9a6d-7aa80d9c0464', '2026-07-24', true, null, 'I learned about the finance department''s methods
ON cost awareness AND TCO.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-24 06:34:52.51885+00', '2026-07-24 06:34:52.51885+00', '1.5'), ('5a4e8c6c-32ad-40e6-8d33-b60c5a43ce82', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '87d95890-025b-4bb3-98fc-d9452c8c724f', '2026-07-14', true, null, 'I learned more about the recruitment AND selection process IN MATTA, its training courses, AND the difference BETWEEN OJTs AND voluntaries.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-14 08:39:51.917366+00', '2026-07-14 08:39:51.917366+00', '1.0'), ('5f04a35e-ce6b-410e-80f6-98cf808a4691', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '4f240a0b-2e26-4613-b581-db1db4083b8f', '2026-08-18', true, '94.00', 'Notes: Course 2 introduced the key indicators used to measure Production Department performance, organized around Quality, Cost, AND Delivery (QCD). Quality is tracked through DPU (defects per unit, target 0%) AND NPR (number of problem reports
FROM customers, target 0), both checked usually monthly. Cost is tracked through labor cost per unit hour,
WITH a target of 97 against a minimum of 75 plus overhead. Delivery covers routing down rate, production efficiency (target 0.89, the ratio of completed routing time to attendance time), AND the work order closing cycle (target 16 days). The session also introduced lean manufacturing, which focuses
ON lessening waste IN the form of idle time, material travel, downtime, AND loss time. Reflection: These indicators give me a concrete way to understand what “good performance” actually looks like
ON the production floor, beyond just following instructions. AS a MATTA trainee, I will eventually be expected to interpret data LIKE DPU, NPR, AND work order cycle times, so being able to read these numbers now, AND understand what drives them, prepares me to contribute more meaningfully once I am assigned real responsibilities. It also reinforces the choice-before-effort mindset
FROM Sir Yangson’s session: knowing the target numbers first helps me work backward toward the right actions, instead of just staying busy without knowing whether I am actually improving quality, cost, or delivery.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:14:58.280127+00', '2026-08-21 05:17:01.760679+00', '2.0'), ('69d630ee-6af4-4fd1-8f7f-a1fabd095d67', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'efa0519a-a250-4072-b49c-8388ec997a3c', '2026-07-17', true, null, 'Here I learned more in-depth about BROWAVES products, the production line, AND their processes.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-17 07:15:49.935683+00', '2026-07-17 07:15:49.935683+00', '1.5'), ('6f143977-9b8a-4bf6-bd28-c3ed1c1da39f', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'c32ad98d-50a9-4df7-9a90-7a882928de60', '2026-08-14', true, null, 'I learned about the Daisi machine operation.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-14 07:27:27.208637+00', '2026-08-14 07:27:27.208637+00', '8.0'), ('70ab8387-3456-4159-b353-5d11fd340940', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '15386425-83d4-4200-ac1c-953d3bf6edf4', '2026-08-25', true, null, 'Reflection: Working through this case reminded me how much a management associate’s effectiveness depends
ON the ability to think through a problem methodically rather than jumping straight to a solution. Case analysis forced me to slow down, gather the full picture, AND separate symptoms
FROM the actual root cause before recommending anything. That discipline matters because AS a MATTA trainee, I will constantly be handed incomplete or conflicting information
FROM different departments, AND the quality of my decisions will depend
ON how well I can structure that information into a clear problem statement, test possible causes, AND verify that a fix actually works instead of just masking the issue temporarily. Beyond the technical process, this exercise also showed me why documentation AND communication are inseparable
FROM analysis itself. A correct root cause is only useful if it is reported clearly AND acted
ON quickly across teams LIKE MI, QC, AND PD. Developing this skill now builds the judgment I will need to lead cross-functional problem-solving, prevent recurring issues instead of repeatedly firefighting them, AND make sound, defensible recommendations AS I take
ON more responsibility.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-25 03:51:14.648479+00', '2026-08-25 03:51:23.99003+00', '2.0'), ('731e61e6-f140-4cae-8972-c4cf8eb46465', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '29617875-9d12-4b24-b9e1-58ee51519baa', '2026-07-15', true, null, 'Here I learned tips about what makes a PowerPoint presentation look good AND readable to an audience.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-15 08:23:44.918294+00', '2026-07-15 08:23:44.918294+00', '1.5'), ('73e1ed4f-c39e-4983-9f8a-d6ae15de055a', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'ce1a50e5-9345-4397-822c-f5184ea267a5', '2026-08-07', true, null, 'I learned about the glue curing process, the baking tables AND its forms.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-07 07:22:15.179+00', '2026-08-07 07:22:15.179+00', '8.0'), ('7858dfdd-6b3a-4139-ad37-4b898b881ff7', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '85ee61ae-ab16-4090-b7a5-7f8a318bfd30', '2026-08-20', true, null, 'Notes: Course 10, Choice Before Effort, framed life AS a series of decisions at critical moments, described AS the “three exams of life” at ages 30, 40, AND 50. At 30, the goal is to have moved beyond entry-level pay AND to be leading IN some capacity. At 40, the focus shifts to being a strategic decision maker AND starting retirement planning, while balancing responsibilities to aging parents AND growing children. At 50, the goal becomes financial freedom AND legacy, working
FROM passion rather than survival,
WITH liberty AS the keyword for that next chapter. Sir Yangson stressed that age is not equal to success but time is equal to promotion, that choice matters more than effort, that direction determines destiny, AND closed
WITH an action plan: define your age 30 goal, optimize your current path, AND prioritize strategic choices OVER tactical busyness. Reflection: Of everything covered this week, this session had the strongest impact
ON how I want to approach the rest of my MATTA training. It reframed my responsibilities not just AS tasks to complete, but AS choices that either move me toward or away
FROM a direction I actually want. Applying the action plan to myself AS a trainee, my version of “defining my age 30 goal” is figuring out what kind of professional I want to be by the time I finish this program, “optimizing my current path” means checking whether each rotation AND each skill I am building is actually serving that goal, AND “prioritizing strategic choices OVER tactical busyness” means resisting the urge to just stay busy completing requirements without asking whether they are building toward something. This is the mindset I plan to carry into every week of the program
FROM here on.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:45:58.127078+00', '2026-08-21 00:45:58.127078+00', '1.0'), ('79d0d339-301e-403a-b781-572fe735ae66', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '5d66fd54-95f8-48cb-83a7-3a14250d0fbb', '2026-08-20', true, null, 'Notes: This course covered how AI AND enterprise applications support the business, starting
WITH what enterprise applications generally require: high scalability AND availability, unified data AND systems, strict security AND compliance, AND customizability through rules. It THEN focused
ON two core systems: ERP (Enterprise Resource Planning), built
ON an ORACLE database AND module covering purchasing procurement, HR, finance, business intelligence, AND CRM, AND Lotus Notes, used for communication AND scheduling, custom rapid apps, a document-oriented database, office replication, AND granular security. An important distinction was that Lotus Notes cannot directly transfer or exchange data
WITH ERP, AND instead relies
ON an “Open with” function,
WITH databases identified AS DS31, DS32, AND ERP. Reflection: This session gave me a glimpse of the digital backbone that supports everything else I learned this week,
FROM the key indicators IN Course 2 to the warehouse process IN Course 7, since systems LIKE ERP are likely
WHERE much of that data actually lives
AND gets tracked. AS a MATTA trainee, I do not expect to be managing these systems directly yet, but understanding that different departments (HR, Finance, Procurement, CRM) all run through a shared ERP structure helps me see why cross-functional collaboration, which came up repeatedly this week, matters so much IN practice. It also reminded me that even something AS technical AS enterprise software ultimately exists to support people making better, faster decisions, which ties back to the direction-and-goal-setting theme running through this whole first week.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:49:25.657308+00', '2026-08-21 05:16:15.915569+00', '2.0'), ('7ca8dbba-e653-4609-9f9b-cf8a39ad4292', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '920332a0-9aa1-473d-a34b-a34452befe47', '2026-07-23', true, null, 'On the topic of AI: "78% of Filipino workers use AI at work but few receive training — study" Link: https://www.msn.com/en-ph/technology/artificial-intelligence/78-of-filipino-workers-use-ai-at-work-but-few-receive-training-study/ar-AA28pz3u?ocid = socialshare Reflections: It''s good to see the technology get adapted by different industries IN the country but if they don''t receive proper training about it, it could make the users too dependent
ON it without knowing how to use it AS an assist instead of fully relying
ON AI.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-23 00:36:08.965479+00', '2026-07-23 00:36:08.965479+00', '1.0'), ('7e47738f-8e9e-4f86-a344-cbf461ff1c5e', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '335a63fd-03f7-4de7-8913-82e8e768b220', '2026-07-24', true, null, 'Here I was given a brief introduction to PDCA, the 5 Whys, the fishbone method, AND FMEA (failure mode AND effects analysis)', 'in_progress', '2026-07-24 09:01:35.10776+00', '2026-07-24 09:01:35.10776+00', '2.0'), ('811e2bf7-d664-43d7-8563-0a992ff7a308', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '5d0c70d6-7bd8-44fd-b685-ba5959e9fd92', '2026-07-20', true, null, 'I learned about the PDCA AND how to apply it to my daily life.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-20 08:01:32.018089+00', '2026-07-20 08:01:32.018089+00', '2.0'), ('844f776b-2a1d-4f56-afb5-5de1e712589e', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', 'db3fe185-2935-4101-ac12-1e065564a51e', '2026-08-19', true, null, 'Notes: Course 4 introduced Browave (short for Broadband AND Lightwave) AND the MATTA program itself, which runs through a two-week Phase I Common Core Curriculum, covering morning readings
ON global politics, economy, AI, AND communications, training courses, a learning reflection summary, portfolio maintenance, AND an assessment, followed by a 24-week Phase II of professional training
WITH its own learning portfolio AND QCC (Quality Control Cycle) assessment. It also clarified the difference BETWEEN ODM, OEM, AND CM AS manufacturing arrangements. Reflection: Learning how the MATTA program itself is structured, Phase I building the foundation AND Phase II building professional depth through QCC, helps me see this first week AS just the starting point of a much longer, deliberately designed path rather than a series of disconnected sessions. Knowing the ODM, OEM, AND CM distinctions also gives me a clearer sense of the different ways Browave works
WITH its clients, which I expect will matter once I am assigned to a specific department.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:32:49.184522+00', '2026-08-21 00:40:20.78397+00', '1.0'), ('84f77f88-5301-4bc7-9ae9-38f205eb7c94', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '5228abf3-9f97-4774-bf23-986a920aaae0', '2026-08-24', true, null, 'Summary of Notes: This session introduced leverage AS the multiplier that turns effort into outsized results, contrasting traditional work (1 unit of effort = 1 unit of result)
WITH leveraged work (1 unit of work = 10x result),
WHERE one’s expertise is the fulcrum
AND tools, team,
AND processes are the lever. It outlined three levels of leverage: digital leverage, USING AI
AND automation to turn repeatable tasks into templates or systems; people leverage, tapping collective intelligence by asking for help, knowing who to ask,
AND treating one’s manager AS a resource rather than just an authority;
AND structure leverage, redesigning task ownership, meeting cadence,
AND reporting flows instead of just patching recurring problems,
AND building focus through batching
AND rhythm. It closed 
WITH a reminder to measure oneself by talent, the value created, rather than manpower, the hours logged, AND to proactively seek out leverage instead of waiting for instructions. Reflection: This lecture redefines something I’ve been doing almost by instinct, automating repetitive tasks, building small systems, AS an actual strategy rather than just a personal habit, which is validating but also pushes me to be more deliberate about it AS a MATTA trainee. The idea that working hard IN the wrong direction is the biggest waste of talent hits close to home; I want to make sure I’m not just staying busy but actually building leverage, especially now while I’m still figuring out
WHERE my effort matters most. The people leverage point is the one I find hardest to internalize: my instinct AS a new trainee is to struggle through problems alone rather than ask, partly because I don’t want to seem unprepared, but this session makes me see upward management
AND asking for help AS a skill to practice rather than a weakness. I also want to hold
ON to the manpower-versus-talent distinction, since it’s easy for a trainee to equate long hours
WITH value, AND I’d rather measure my own progress by what I actually produce AND improve, not just time spent at my desk.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-24 07:52:09.950127+00', '2026-08-24 07:52:09.950127+00', '1.0'), ('8a668817-daa4-4482-bb67-720203a5fd5a', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'c3e6b957-8684-4b4e-9cb0-0aaf16a2d4e5', '2026-07-20', true, null, 'On the topic of Politics: "PH reviews ICC cooperation after US call to dismantle tribunal -Palace" Link: https://globalnation.inquirer.net/331007/ph-reviews-icc-cooperation-after-us-call-to-dismantle-tribunal-palace Reflections: The ICC is there for the powerless, I don''t know why a global superpower such AS US would want to dismantle something that is serving for the betterment of the world. They are not even part of the ICC, but the country right now is notorious for their horrible leaders AND heinous crimes.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-20 00:17:44.678009+00', '2026-07-20 00:17:44.678009+00', '1.0'), ('8c4faa5c-1c04-41fa-88b4-6d5be4ff5b55', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '0435bcb7-6446-43b2-96fb-0588937e7382', '2026-07-13', true, null, 'I learned about Sir Yangson''s life AND ambitions, AND he gave me a lot of things to learn. He empasized the importance of setting your own goal first to be able to properly work AND give effort for it, to have integrity IN the workplace, to make the decision before doing any form of effort, how to merge your life AND career to keep the passion alive, AND more general things about adult mindset.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-14 01:23:25.246277+00', '2026-07-15 05:19:01.947674+00', '2.5'), ('8d6d3cb5-4b14-4ce6-b507-1592dd293b66', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'd3854ae3-e15d-4a4a-a384-770baded2553', '2026-08-21', true, null, 'I learned about the parts being assembled AND the steps of how to install parts such AS the housing, pin keeper AND the dust cap.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 08:15:09.907047+00', '2026-08-21 08:15:09.907047+00', '8.0'), ('935f8dd4-f583-4914-a08c-44d4d1ab737d', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'ffd3503e-a87e-409a-acb9-7339b297e90c', '2026-07-13', true, null, 'Here I learned about how the company name became "BROWAVE", its site of operations, how the company made the choice to have their third branch here IN the Philippines, their products, their mission of BROWAVE for their products to reach the rest of the world, its involvement
WITH AI technology AND NVIDIA, AND their safety certifications. I also learned more about the MATTA program, its courses, AND how it aims to make leaders to be the bridge for the rest of the world.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-14 01:28:18.778736+00', '2026-07-14 01:29:31.691783+00', '2.0'), ('996f1080-85f2-4731-a0c3-88a133ef0372', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '60068a65-c765-4317-9656-6b6e3937e9af', '2026-07-14', true, null, 'I learned about the role of ISO into maintaining standards
ON specific aspects such AS quality control AND environmental protection. I also learned about the PDCA (Plan, Do, Check, Action) approach used IN most of the encounters IN the industry. I also learned that quality is not necessarily a perfect product but it is for customer satisfaction.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-14 08:32:53.807568+00', '2026-07-15 05:19:38.684491+00', '2.0'), ('9ea14eb9-3f69-47d1-8b3f-3a4b0227847e', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '5451bf91-79e4-443c-8465-147f7990a046', '2026-08-20', true, null, 'I observed the final end face inspection AND saw what methods they use to get rid of dirt, debris AND defects.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 08:12:51.912818+00', '2026-08-21 08:12:51.912818+00', '8.0'), ('9ed162cd-5d16-4966-aa04-56c22ce0bf41', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '9f85d205-ab10-4b92-991b-d9caa4b7e06e', '2026-08-24', true, null, 'Notes: According to Apollo Global Management chief economist Torsten Slok AND researcher Sania Edlich, AI’s impact is showing up more IN wage growth than IN overall employment. Their study examined roughly 300 occupations, grouping them into high- AND low-AI-exposure categories, AND compared how each group fared before AND after the introduction of ChatGPT. The results showed that wages for workers IN high-AI-exposure roles grew 6.7% more slowly than those IN low-exposure roles,
WITH the effect most pronounced among lower-income workers. Despite this wage pressure, AI has accelerated the rate of business formation, which is now at a record high, AS it allows people to generate ideas AND build businesses more easily.
ON the employment side, fields highly exposed to AI substitution saw a faster decline IN job openings than other industries, AND AI’s reach continues to widen across workplaces: 37% of surveyed workers reported that their employer had introduced new AI or automation tools within the past 12 months. Reflection: This raises an important point: the convenience AI brings seems to be slowing wage growth rather than eliminating jobs outright. This may be because once an automation system is IN place, the workload shifts
FROM performing repetitive tasks to simply reviewing the output, reducing the need to raise pay for that role. However, it is also worth noting that some jobs see this AS additional work, since fact-checking requires extra time. While many assume AI’s biggest threat is job replacement, the more pressing issue may actually be stagnant wages. Full-scale automation has not yet arrived, but the decline already visible IN wages could eventually translate into higher unemployment if no action plan is put IN place. What is especially concerning is that minimum-wage earners are the most affected, which should prompt the government to consider assistance for this group. Lower-income workers are also receiving less training, reporting less confidence, AND have fewer financial buffers to absorb the impact of this disruption.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-24 00:31:09.515628+00', '2026-08-24 04:49:45.95192+00', '0.5'), ('a0b278d2-cca8-4c18-a431-3c57fad07b91', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '9cdeb70e-6c28-4ec4-9276-c13b35a59605', '2026-07-30', true, null, 'I learned about the other specifications AND forms used IN the cutting AND temperature cycling process AND my introduction to the batch feeding process begins.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-05 09:19:35.434693+00', '2026-08-05 09:19:35.434693+00', '8.0'), ('a59190d4-cb19-4518-b835-cd1fd83baba1', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '3cbc106e-005b-4eef-8cd5-d796f74893a8', '2026-08-24', true, null, 'Notes: DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara said the department is working to ensure Filipino students are equipped
WITH strong reading, writing, AND math skills while preparing them for a future IN which artificial intelligence (AI) will be part of everyday life AND work. While some students already use AI to complete assignments, Angara noted that the bigger challenge is helping both learners AND teachers understand how to use the technology responsibly AS it becomes more common across industries, since technology cannot make up for weak learning fundamentals. To help close these gaps, DepEd’s Academic Recovery AND Accessible Learning (ARAL) Program, now IN its second year, provides tutorials to help struggling learners catch up AND become ready for the next grade level. The department has also allotted more time for teacher training by shifting
FROM four academic terms to three, allowing educators to attend professional development programs without losing classroom instruction time, AND is expanding online training IN digital AND information technology skills. Beyond academics, DepEd is working to reduce stress IN schools by creating more peaceful learning environments, IN line
WITH the President’s push for safer schools, AND is addressing the shortage of guidance counselors by hiring guidance counselor associates to provide additional support for learners. The department is likewise stepping up efforts against functional illiteracy by funding reading projects IN low-performing municipalities, increasing the supply of books IN schools, AND reviewing teaching methods so that the focus shifts
FROM memorizing lessons to actually understanding AND applying what students read. AS Angara put it, the core challenge remains “the ability to read AND to comprehend” — functional literacy — which he named AS the department’s main focus going forward. Reflection: I agree
WITH Angara that the challenge really comes down to the basics. However, reading comprehension AND literacy struggles among Filipino students have been a long-standing problem well before the emergence of AI. Applying the “5 whys” approach helps trace the issue to its root: children struggle
WITH reading AND writing because they have weak foundations, which stem
FROM limited teacher materials AND resources, which IN turn stem
FROM an imbalanced student-to-teacher ratio, which stems
FROM a shortage of teachers, which ultimately comes down to pay that is not sustainable relative to the workload required. That may be one of the underlying causes, AND it reinforces the idea that a problem cannot truly be solved without first identifying the root cause of the main issue. Another concern is a policy that does not allow students to be held back even WHEN they have not yet mastered the skills required for their grade level, meaning learners can advance without a solid foundation. Addressing this may require focusing
ON strengthening foundational skills specifically
FROM kindergarten through grade 6.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-24 01:16:08.434316+00', '2026-08-24 04:50:08.766805+00', '0.5'), ('a78f9d07-b2e5-42a8-be08-769faf669ccb', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '920332a0-9aa1-473d-a34b-a34452befe47', '2026-07-21', true, null, 'On the topic of AI: "Nvidia’s Jensen Huang just declared the ''next frontier'' of AI—and it''s not chatbots" Here, Huang is talking about robots being the next frontier of AI. Link: https://www.msn.com/en-us/money/smallbusiness/nvidia-s-jensen-huang-just-declared-the-next-frontier-of-ai-and-it-s-not-chatbots/ar-AA28ccp7?ocid = socialshare "AI company hit by hack entirely done by artificial intelligence" Link: https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/technology/ai-company-hit-by-hack-entirely-done-by-artificial-intelligence/ar-AA28juzj?ocid = socialshare Reflection: Here I read two different kinds of news regarding AI, one is an optimistic one AND one is a scary one because it shows the potential of AI being used for bad things.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-21 00:23:53.997536+00', '2026-07-21 00:23:53.997536+00', '1.0'), ('aa136c1e-05a2-44d6-87a1-0756f8893946', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '7162934d-2b71-4f00-b732-506227d82753', '2026-08-19', true, null, 'I observed the operators do their end face inspections AND learned about the different appearances of defects.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-20 09:00:04.348309+00', '2026-08-20 09:00:04.348309+00', '8.0'), ('ab53220c-3e59-4e55-828b-de9ea7435e2f', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', 'b17b0228-7faf-477a-a7c0-a43d9b98575e', '2026-08-19', true, null, 'Notes: Course 5 taught a goal-first way of thinking, starting
FROM the goal AND working backward to what to do AND what one currently has, rather than starting
FROM what one already has. Key points included that self-alignment is important, that passion plus ambition leads to success, that choice should come before effort, AND that effort IN the wrong direction is wasted. Reflection: This course’s goal-first framework changed how I want to approach the rest of the program. Instead of just moving
FROM one scheduled activity to the next, I want to keep asking what my goal for this traineeship actually is, AND let that shape how I engage
WITH each phase, each rotation, AND each responsibility I am eventually given.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:34:35.939157+00', '2026-08-21 00:34:35.939157+00', '1.0'), ('ab568e4a-9cff-4dc3-a0a9-e063a27f10f0', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'd783d38e-b399-4ed1-864b-1174f879b4c8', '2026-07-14', true, null, 'Here I learned about survival tips IN the office/workplace, the "survival of the fittest" concept conveyed through the Law of the Jungle, AND the Five Things -- Time Management, Emotional Management, Professional Distance
WITH coworkers, Observational skills AND Adaptability, AND Focusing
ON Work Performance. I also learned about communicating through email AND how to properly achieve your goals.'{comma} 'in_progress'{comma} '2026-07-14 08:36:57.466017+00'{comma} '2026-07-15 05:19:26.761523+00'{comma} '2.0'){comma} ('ad05c992-9297-41e4-84fa-f5ca57dfe8a0'{comma} '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548'{comma} 'e0ce5018-af1c-4b05-bd1e-97e686b81b05'{comma} '2026-08-21'{comma} true{comma} null{comma} 'Notes: This course covered how to analyze AND respond to manufacturing abnormalities. A manufacturing abnormality is defined by a product not meeting specifications or a process deviating
FROM the standard, which may cause customer complaints AND requires immediate investigation plus preventive AND corrective action. Problem analysis matters because it prevents defective products
FROM reaching customers, identifies the root cause rather than just the symptom, improves product quality AND process reliability, reduces scrap, rework, AND production cost, AND supports continuous improvement. The session introduced the 8 Disciplines (8D) framework: team formation, problem description, interim containment (including identifying other affected products), defining AND verifying the root cause, corrective action, verification of effectiveness, preventive measures, AND finally congratulating the team. It also covered forming a cross-functional team within production (not including warehouse), AND emphasized that problem-solving must be data-driven, root-cause-verified, standardized, continuously improved, AND prevention-focused, closing
WITH the principle that you should not just correct the defect, but eliminate the cause, strengthen the process, AND prevent recurrence. 
 Reflection: AS a MATTA trainee, this course offers a discipline that extends far beyond the production floor, approaching any problem, whether it''s a defective product or a slip-up IN my own training tasks, AS something to be diagnosed rather than simply patched over. The 8D framework''s emphasis
ON forming a team AND bringing IN cross-functional input before going to a fix pushes back against the trainee instinct to solve things quickly AND alone. It''s a reminder that even a technical issue is a coordination challenge. The most important takeaway
FROM this course is probably the line "do not just correct the defect, eliminate the cause, strengthen the process, and prevent recurrence," since it applies directly to my own mistakes during training: instead of fixing something once AND moving forward, I should be asking what gap or habit allowed it to happen, AND what change would actually stop it
FROM happening again. Building the habit of verifying root causes
WITH data rather than assumptions is exactly the kind of discipline I want to develop early
ON AS a trainee.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-22 06:45:19.613712+00', '2026-08-22 06:45:19.613712+00', '2.0'), ('adcc59aa-9b24-4956-b4f8-0c7b0657d8bd', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '13d4bcee-d573-4643-a437-0c211f02bc04', '2026-07-23', true, null, 'I learned about Eastern AND Western cultures, their similarities AND differences AND how to speak a few Mandarin phrases.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-23 07:25:59.141817+00', '2026-07-23 07:25:59.141817+00', '2.0'), ('ae8fd4c3-e0f7-4072-93f6-81ef988abef4', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '215877bf-d026-4fff-8037-3f1f6c4f2fd0', '2026-08-24', true, null, 'Summary of Notes: This session covered how to design clear, effective PowerPoint slides for briefing executives, grounded IN the data-information-knowledge-wisdom hierarchy AND the 5W1H approach to organizing content logically. The key principles are accuracy, clarity, AND simplicity, applied through practical layout rules: keep text brief, use consistent fonts AND sizes (32pt for titles, 20pt for body text), use color purposefully (cool tones for presenting information, warm tones for promotion), favor charts AND icons OVER dense text, AND leave enough white space. Reflection: AS a MATTA trainee, I’ll likely be asked to prepare slides or reports for supervisors, so these layout AND clarity principles directly shape how I deliver information for people who need to act
ON it quickly. I notice I tend to overload slides
WITH detail WHEN I’m worried about leaving something out, so the reminder to keep text concise AND let visuals LIKE charts carry information is something I want to consciously practice. This also ties back to what I learned about Taiwanese workplace culture: busy executives value efficiency, so a clean, easy-to-scan slide is itself a way of respecting their time.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-24 05:44:12.290364+00', '2026-08-24 05:44:12.290364+00', '0.5'), ('b1159cd9-5492-44e6-aa09-7c3e50047df6', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'c43abbcf-1244-48b0-b048-436689c591a1', '2026-07-22', true, null, 'I learned about the coordination BETWEEN Planning AND the Warehouse to ensure smooth production AND customer satisfaction.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-22 07:48:44.863025+00', '2026-07-22 07:48:44.863025+00', '2.0'), ('b464b18c-f08f-4596-aa99-77b7c2ed422a', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'a9f12747-ac1d-4037-8a7d-893a6dbe53da', '2026-07-20', true, null, 'Here, I was given pointers
ON how to improve my report writing skills.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-20 02:31:19.569928+00', '2026-07-20 02:31:19.569928+00', '1.5'), ('b6df91bf-b429-4b77-88d1-4c0559a03e72', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'c2402084-c2cf-4bf7-976e-a063ceac14c0', '2026-07-13', true, null, 'On the topic of AI: Zhipu released GLM-5.2 AS open source software, AS its founder Tang Jie argued that AI should stay accessible for everyone than controlled by a
SELECT  few. Link: https://thenextweb.com/news/zhipu-tang-jie-frontier-ai-open-to-all
ON the topic of Global Politics: "Iran''s supreme leader calls for revenge in new message as US-Iran strikes continue" Link: https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/world/iran-s-supreme-leader-calls-for-revenge-in-new-message-as-us-iran-strikes-continue/vi-AA27KPeu?ocid = msedgntphdr&cvid = a2b40d8e95914c388233d7f3f13d1849&cvpid = eedc430e5fd04bdf8cc02ea3c4b42ce8&ei = 7#details Reflections: AI technology is indeed a powerful tool that improves life IN so many ways, it''s selfish to restrict other people
FROM being able to access it. Global politics makes me sad most of the time. I hope these wars end, it''s affecting everyone AND there''s nothing good to get
FROM wars.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-14 01:04:21.95801+00', '2026-07-14 01:36:40.182428+00', '1.0'), ('b880df8c-88a5-44a6-9ae4-bfcca21098fd', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'f55a1d44-6ecc-48ac-b724-b54d9cb4d8fc', '2026-07-21', true, null, 'Here I was taught about storytelling techniques AND AI tools to

CREATE a more compelling presentation.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-21 07:34:20.405131+00', '2026-07-21 07:34:20.405131+00', '2.0'), ('b8f05897-821c-4d7e-9046-b94a6a18da73', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '7feaac81-2676-4a28-a234-82d581562a02', '2026-08-25', true, null, 'Notes:The article frames AI AS a “significant but manageable” threat to the Philippine BPO industry: it will not wipe out the sector, but it will slow employment growth, AND entry-level, rules-based work (customer inquiries, password resets, data entry, transcription, scheduling, templated chat/email support) is most exposed because it is repetitive AND standardized. Roles built
ON judgment, accountability, empathy, domain expertise, AND complex problem-solving are more resilient. IBPAP’s response is not to resist AI but to turn the Philippines into an AI-enabled BPO hub, attracting global capability centers IN tech, finance, analytics, cybersecurity, AND engineering, AND diversifying beyond traditional markets. The tradeoff is that AI infrastructure, LIKE data centers, consumes heavy amounts of water, land, AND other resources. Upskilling alone will not close the gap either, since employers mostly train people for their current role rather than a new one, so the piece calls for government-backed reskilling (portable credentials, updated TESDA AND university curricula, apprenticeships, job matching, transition assistance) plus ongoing research into
WHERE new opportunities emerge. Reflection: This reading captured my interest because I just graduated,
AND I really am fortunate enough to get a job immediately. I know that there is an employment problem existing due to the emergence of AI, but reading it 
WITH backed-up references really made the problem, IN a way, real. I belong to people looking for entry-level jobs AND aside
FROM AI, people
WITH more experience than I am are also my competitors IN the job market. Hence, it made me thankful to the company for risking AND putting their trust IN me even though I have little experience to offer. Also, IN the text, it was mentioned that upskilling alone is not enough. This is
WHERE I realized that sometimes, the problem cannot solely be solved by the people involved. There is really a need for intervention by the government. It’s easier to blame the people for this, but the problem is not really for us workers to solve but rather by the government. Now, AS a MATTA trainee, this reading is a preview of the environment I will eventually manage people in. Entry-level
AND process-heavy work is exactly
WHERE many new hires start, so AS a future manager I need to watch which tasks
ON my team are repetitive AND automatable versus which require judgment, AND start coaching people toward the second category early instead of waiting for restructuring to force it. It also changes how I think about training: since companies mostly train employees for the job that exists rather than the job that is coming, part of my role will be to build IN stretch assignments, cross-training, AND exposure to ambiguous problems (like the case analysis exercise) so my team develops transferable skills, critical thinking, complex problem-solving, empathy IN customer AND employee interactions, rather than narrow task competence that AI can absorb. Positioning myself AND my future team toward AI-augmented, higher-value work rather than IN competition
WITH AI is a leadership responsibility, not just an individual one. I will need to communicate that shift clearly AND help my team see AI AS a tool that raises the bar
ON judgment AND expertise, not just a threat to headcount.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-25 05:25:27.011765+00', '2026-08-25 05:25:27.011765+00', '0.5'), ('bfad770b-4ef2-4bbf-bdef-0ec6ca342361', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '20b09d8e-7589-4fa2-8666-0f3b360e1bab', '2026-07-21', true, null, 'Here I learned about the three stages
WHERE you have to have obtained a certain

SET of skills AND earning power, to be able to live life smoothly IN retirement.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-21 02:22:20.560118+00', '2026-07-21 02:22:20.560118+00', '2.0'), ('c25f0cf0-76fb-4022-a8bf-4230401b20cf', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '693f6acd-e5a9-4c53-aa1b-41caf791cd22', '2026-07-29', true, null, 'I learned about the specifications of the cutting AND winding process, general process of temperature cycling AND how to access the travelcard printing system.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-05 09:13:59.848849+00', '2026-08-06 08:55:16.693263+00', '8.0'), ('c4b063e3-c15f-4cfc-ad6f-03e45705411e', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'ae1f14ba-c11a-4397-ba3f-8309b5a67dc6', '2026-07-15', true, null, 'Here I learned about the warehouse AND how it functions, also how it collaborates
WITH different departments to be able to receive raw materials AND ship out finished goods AS best AS they can. I was also given a tour of the warehouse
WHERE I saw the materials,
WHERE they receive boxes of raw materials,
WHERE they track each individual item that enters the warehouse,
AND
WHERE they store them.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-15 06:24:12.857862+00', '2026-07-15 06:24:23.827293+00', '2.0'), ('cd9fcbaf-a037-45ef-8f62-4209a9b4c518', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'af9bc4a2-1c53-4997-a30d-2f84ef3431db', '2026-07-22', true, null, 'I learned about the pillars of leverage
AND what to do to utilize it.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-22 07:07:41.488289+00', '2026-07-22 07:09:03.783624+00', '2.0'), ('cf88c706-b03b-4fdd-9202-d6d3dd463ea2', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '00caf629-1087-4d34-b1e5-081ec3002ba1', '2026-07-13', true, null, 'Here I learned about the different personal productivity styles, how time is perceived by different types of people, how to manage time properly USING the Eisenhower Matrix to be able to properly arrage tasks by priority
AND urgency, the importance of assigning leaders, clear targets
AND a scheduled deadline,
AND how to get people to do what you need to do -- by giving them a benefit
FROM said action.'{comma} 'in_progress'{comma} '2026-07-14 01:29:53.815357+00'{comma} '2026-07-15 05:18:45.376325+00'{comma} '2.5'){comma} ('da7e0198-87db-43fd-934c-a293ee00b524'{comma} 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57'{comma} 'bb6c44f7-3950-423d-b485-e3ad3034e8af'{comma} '2026-08-06'{comma} true{comma} null{comma} 'I learned about the automatic stripping macine for exposing bare fiber, the steps
ON how to do the through fiber process AND its specifications.'{comma} 'in_progress'{comma} '2026-08-07 07:20:35.444432+00'{comma} '2026-08-07 07:20:35.444432+00'{comma} '8.0'){comma} ('dc140b35-6f2f-4b21-b112-b20870d39f35'{comma} 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57'{comma} '6217f6d3-8f24-44f6-834e-741f2abb7ec4'{comma} '2026-07-22'{comma} true{comma} null{comma} 'I learned about the Production Line, their process, AND what each sections do.'{comma} 'in_progress'{comma} '2026-07-22 07:08:52.561383+00'{comma} '2026-07-22 07:08:52.561383+00'{comma} '2.0'){comma} ('ddd3e3d7-05ce-4b34-9cc0-a99e08f710f7'{comma} '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548'{comma} '1b48372b-a866-4f03-86e0-869563784e63'{comma} '2026-08-24'{comma} true{comma} null{comma} 'Summary of Notes: 
 This session outlined the core competencies for professional effectiveness: professional competence AS the overlap of attitude, knowledge, AND skills, expressed through communication, organization, AND problem solving. Good communication rests
ON clarity, accuracy, AND two-way interaction, matched to the right method AND delivery. Organization follows a data collection, verification, analysis, AND recommendation flow, while problem solving follows the IDEAL model (identify, define, explore, act, look back AND learn). Efficient work comes down to clear goal setting, time management, AND prioritizing tasks, AND demonstrating this competence ultimately means accurately delivering results, offering valuable suggestions, thinking systematically, AND building one’s personal brand. Reflection: This session feels LIKE a toolkit I can start applying right away AS a trainee still building my work habits. The IDEAL problem-solving framework gives me a concrete process to fall back
ON instead of jumping straight to a solution, which is a habit I want to build early. I also recognize that prioritizing tasks AND managing time well are still skills I’m developing, so
HAVING a simple checklist for efficiency makes it feel more achievable day to day. The point about building a personal brand through consistent, reliable results stands out to me too, since AS a new trainee, how I handle small tasks now likely shapes how my supervisors see me going forward. Since Browave values efficiency AND speed
WITH quality, AS I learned IN the culture session, I see this course AS giving me the practical skills to actually meet that expectation, not just understand it culturally.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-24 05:45:21.486901+00', '2026-08-24 05:45:59.353716+00', '1.0'), ('e0c4f9e4-f73c-4607-a3c6-080f4be650a3', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', 'd1aaaf87-b24b-4cc2-8588-ffc8826f71f6', '2026-08-24', true, null, 'Summary of Notes: This session introduced PDCA (Plan-Do-Check-Act) AS a continuous cycle for problem-solving. Planning starts by distinguishing the actual problem
FROM its symptoms USING tools LIKE the 5 Whys AND the fishbone diagram, THEN setting SMART goals (specific, measurable, achievable, relevant, time-based). Doing means executing the plan, while Checking relies
ON data rather than impressions, comparing before-and-after results AND analyzing both successes AND failures. Acting determines whether the improvement is actually sustained, closing the loop before the same problem resurfaces. Reflection PDCA feels LIKE a more structured version of the IDEAL framework
FROM the operational efficiency session, AND
HAVING both gives me a couple of concrete lenses to apply instead of just reacting to problems AS they come up. The distinction BETWEEN a problem AND its symptom stands out to me because I think, AS a new trainee, I’m more likely to notice AND want to fix the visible symptom without digging into the 5 Whys or root cause, since that takes more time AND confidence to do properly. I also want to take the Check stage seriously AND get comfortable relying
ON data OVER my own impressions, since it’s easy to assume something worked because it felt LIKE it did. Overall, this gives me a repeatable process I can use
ON small tasks now, so that thinking this way becomes a habit well before I’m handling bigger problems
ON my own.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-24 08:12:16.076355+00', '2026-08-24 08:12:16.076355+00', '1.0'), ('e552c367-e7f2-4c1c-9d17-761e57723433', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', 'ac50f79c-c6fc-4c3a-ad25-34d5d2b06281', '2026-08-19', true, null, 'Notes: This course covered 5M1E, a root-cause problem-solving methodology used to reduce defects, improve productivity, standardize processes, support continuous improvement, AND prevent problems
FROM recurring. It breaks a problem down into six possible cause categories: Man (training, human error, fatigue, communication, experience, procedure compliance), Machine (settings, worn tools, maintenance, calibration), Material (quality AND specifications of raw materials AND supplies), Method (procedures, SOPs, AND work instructions), Measurement (inspection, calibration, AND data recording accuracy), AND Environment (lighting, humidity, temperature, dust, noise, AND workplace conditions). The session closed
WITH a simple but memorable principle: fix the cause, not the symptom. Reflection: 5M1E gives me a practical checklist I can actually use once I start handling tasks AS a trainee, since it turns “something went wrong” into six specific angles to investigate instead of one vague problem. I noticed it overlaps closely
WITH the Fishbone diagram
FROM Course 3, which reassured me that these frameworks are consistent across the sessions rather than a random collection of tools. More importantly, “fix the cause, not the symptom” feels LIKE the same choice-before-effort principle Sir Yangson emphasized, applied specifically to problem-solving: it is easy to work hard patching symptoms, but real improvement only comes
FROM choosing to look for the actual root cause first.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:44:38.533823+00', '2026-08-21 05:16:52.225204+00', '2.0'), ('ec3a3283-b06f-4356-9981-0a222575ca9a', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '1fd5cc0a-0e24-40a2-ae9e-f0a35c1c0a90', '2026-08-19', true, null, 'Notes: This session went deeper into Browave’s actual products AND manufacturing process. It covered fiber optic technology AND its advantages OVER copper wire (speed, distance, reliability, bandwidth), the difference BETWEEN single-mode fiber (long distance, telecom) AND multi-mode fiber (short distance, data centers AND LANs), AND key components such AS the PLC splitter, fiber optic connectors (SC, LC, ST, MPO types), the optical splitter module, AND WDM filters (Coarse AND Dense,

WITH Add-Drop Filter components LIKE the common, reflect, AND pass ports). It closed
WITH an overview of the end-to-end production workflow, starting
FROM component AND material preparation, AND the departments involved along the way, such AS Mechanical Engineering AND Equipment Maintenance. Reflection: This was the most technical session so far, AND it made me appreciate how many small, precise components go into something AS seemingly simple AS transmitting light through a fiber. AS a MATTA trainee, I think the value of this course is less about memorizing every part name AND more about building a mental map of how a product physically moves
FROM raw material to finished component, since that map will make it much easier to understand
WHERE my future tasks
AND responsibilities actually fit WHEN I get deployed to a department. It also reminded me that behind every key indicator I learned IN Course 2, LIKE quality
AND delivery targets, is an actual physical process 
WITH many steps AND people involved, which makes those numbers feel more real AND less abstract.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:37:28.60472+00', '2026-08-21 05:16:27.192666+00', '2.0'), ('ec6db24f-22fd-4a04-b13c-42a96b43b0d9', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '10e8d843-771e-457b-a3c0-3dee470ab37d', '2026-08-18', true, '17.00', 'Notes: Course 3 covered the QC Seven Tools used for solving complex quality problems: checklists, stratification, Pareto charts, cause-and-effect diagrams, control charts, histograms, AND scatter plots. It also introduced the Fishbone (Ishikawa) diagram for broader problems, which organizes possible causes into Manpower, Method, Machine, Material, Measurement, AND Environment, AND the 5 Whys technique, which is meant for simpler problems AND helps avoid subjectivity by repeatedly asking why an issue occurred until the root cause is found. Reflection: Problem-solving tools LIKE these are directly tied to what I will be expected to do AS a MATTA trainee once I take
ON formal responsibilities, since quality issues will not always have an obvious cause.
HAVING a structured way to approach a problem, starting broad
WITH the Fishbone diagram or narrowing down
WITH the 5 Whys, means I do not have to rely
ON guesswork or intuition alone. This also connects to the idea that choices matter more than effort: USING the right tool for the right kind of problem is itself a choice, AND picking the wrong tool could mean working hard
ON the wrong cause entirely.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:17:37.15259+00', '2026-08-21 05:17:32.363172+00', '1.5'), ('f246e989-777b-4706-851e-79e84fcb7977', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'e96485ca-989b-432d-8bf3-c045b4642186', '2026-08-12', true, null, 'I have tried the SG machine to polish dummy ferrules AND the laser cutting machine.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-13 08:43:20.880828+00', '2026-08-13 08:43:20.880828+00', '8.0'), ('f5f8bb1a-be97-49e7-9a96-fc606dd6fcd1', '61023dbe-ba64-474f-8151-f840d3dc7548', '8084bace-8297-4d40-a82f-69371cf4ed30', '2026-08-19', true, '80.00', 'Notes: The production line tour paired a walkthrough of Browave’s company history (from its roots IN Taiwan, through an expansion into China, to the newer Subic site)
WITH a firsthand look at the products themselves. It reinforced that Browave positions itself around “World Class” quality AND pricing value, AND it introduced the certifications behind that claim, ISO 9001:2015 for Quality Management AND ISO 14001:2015 for Environmental Management. Products were shown AS belonging to three categories (Module, Component, Parts) across four groups (Amplifier Product, Branch Product, WDM, AND OIN), supporting applications such AS FTTH, data centers, CATV, digital media, broadband, AND 5G. Reflection: Walking the actual production line made the earlier, more abstract sessions click into place; the key indicators
FROM Course 2 AND the components
FROM Course 6 are not just concepts
ON a slide, they are what I was seeing move through the line. AS a trainee, I found it useful to actually see how the categories (module, component, parts) AND product groups map onto real stations, since it gives me a clearer picture of
WHERE I might eventually be assigned
AND what quality
AND delivery targets would mean IN that specific area. It also grounded the ISO standards for me: certifications LIKE these are not just compliance requirements, they reflect the same discipline
AND consistency that the earlier quality sessions were building toward.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-21 00:43:05.627912+00', '2026-08-21 05:17:22.161956+00', '2.0'), ('fc2035ed-a792-402a-8a62-e3dd557a5971', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'e18edc8e-c466-4a50-a10c-e5b0857744c3', '2026-08-05', true, null, 'I read work instructions
AND practiced more ribbonization.', 'in_progress', '2026-08-06 08:57:26.766843+00', '2026-08-06 08:57:26.766843+00', '8.0'), ('fc2d6b15-821a-4ea0-ba60-781a38b960e1', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '920332a0-9aa1-473d-a34b-a34452befe47', '2026-07-24', true, null, 'On the topic of AI: "Intel, AMD sign deals with Chinese clients" Link: https://www.msn.com/en-ph/technology/hardware-and-devices/intel-amd-sign-deals-with-chinese-clients/ar-AA28xLpC?ocid = socialshare Reflections: It''s not only GPUs that are getting used en masse for AI technology but also CPUs, AI has already affected prices of these components for the past few years, making it a bit of a struggle to build your own PC because of rising prices.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-24 00:34:42.684273+00', '2026-07-24 00:34:42.684273+00', '1.0'), ('fc75b12f-501f-468b-a917-cc5b56fdd7f1', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', '920332a0-9aa1-473d-a34b-a34452befe47', '2026-07-17', true, null, 'On the Topic of AI: NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang says that AI growth is at the beginning despite worries about it going down. He also visited a Tokyo arcade 
WITH SEGA executives AS thanks to them saving the company IN the ''90s. Link: https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/world/nvidia-s-huang-says-ai-growth-at-beginning-despite-tech-rout/ar-AA280sI2?ocid = socialshare Reflections: AS much AS the advancement IN AI technology is welcome AND if it really is IN its infancy stages, I hope that environmental conservation efforts are also underway to mitigate the effects of maintaining AI data centers.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-17 00:16:52.135787+00', '2026-07-17 00:16:52.135787+00', '1.0'), ('fd4c17c8-e104-44d8-af6a-d901bbe318a8', 'aea42483-c1be-4d6e-a070-c3ac0a33df57', 'f6d33ecc-3e8c-4402-bf3f-ae677ef30d76', '2026-07-15', true, null, 'Here I have learned about the elements of efficiency AS a staff member IN different aspects of communication, presentation, problem solving AND how to build your personal brand IN a professional setting. Tips
ON making a good oral AND visual presentation is also briefly discussed.', 'in_progress', '2026-07-15 03:13:54.826618+00', '2026-07-15 05:20:00.127582+00', '2.0')
